  "9035": {
    "en": [
      "I will not speak to you of sorrow — I have forgotten sorrow at the touch of your hand.",
      "Receiving whatever you have given, Lord, I am content, I am in joy.",
      "This sweet world is a house of joy; that I am here — what tenderness of yours is this —",
      "your moon and your sun rain down their sweet rays.",
      "How many new smiles bloom in the flower groves each day at the new dawn.",
      "Each night, how many planets, how many stars in your silent assembly.",
      "A mother's tenderness, a friend's affection pour nectar in a hundred streams day after day,",
      "the world's honeyed sweetness of love drowns me in a lake of ambrosia.",
      "Small though we are, we know no death; you have given us your fearless refuge,",
      "grief and burning are all taken away at the sight of your feet.",
      "May love grow with every day, may the soul's thirst be quenched each day —",
      "we find new life — new hope wakes in the ever-new new year."
    ],
